  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN266.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">parattaiyiṟ pirintu vantu kūṭiya talaimakaṟkut talaimakaḷ colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What SHE said to HIM who joined [her] after having parted [and] come [back] from the other woman.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN266.1">
        <l>kōṭuṟa nivanta <anchor n="1"/><supplied>nī</supplied>ṭirum parappi</l>
        <l>ṉantīm parāyap putupuṉa ṉerunai</l>
        <l><anchor n="2"/>maintumali kaḷiṟṟiṟ ṟalaippu<supplied>ṇai</supplied> taḻīi</l>
        <l>narantai nāṟuṅ kuvaiyiruṅ kūnta</l>
        <l>liḷantuṇai makaḷirō <supplied>ṭī</supplied>raṇik kalaii</l>
        <l>nīrpeyarn tāṭiya <anchor n="3"/>vēnteḻiṉ maḻaikka</l>
        <l>ṇōkkutoṟu nōkkun tavirvilai yākik</l>
        <l>kāmaṅ kaimikac ciṟa<supplied>t</supplied>tali ṉāṇi<supplied>ḻa</supplied>n</l>
        <l>tāṭiṉai yeṉpa makiḻnaṉai yatuvē</l>
        <l>yāḻi<supplied>cai</supplied> maṟuki ṉī<supplied>ṭūr</supplied> kiḻavōṉ<anchor n="4"/></l>
        <l>vāyvā ḷe<supplied>vvi yē</supplied>vaṉ mēvār </l>
        <l>neṭumiṭal cāytta perumpūṭ poruntava</l>
        <l>rarimmaṇal vā<supplied>yi</supplied> luṟattū rāṅkaṭ</l>
        <l>kaḷḷuṭaip peruñcōṟ <anchor n="5"/>ṟellimi ḻaṉṉa</l>
        <l>kauvaiyā kiṉṟāṟ peritē yi<supplied>ṉiya</supplied>ḵ</l>
        <l>tavala maṉṟuma ṉemakkē vayavar</l>
        <l><anchor n="6"/>kaḻaṉi <supplied>yu</supplied>ḻavar kaliciṟan teṭutta</l>
        <l>ka<supplied>ṟa</supplied>ṅkicai verīip paṟanta tōkai</l>
        <l>yaṇaṅkuṭai varaippakam poliyavan tirukkun</l>
        <l>tirumaṇi viḷakki ṉilaivāyc</l>
        <l>cerumiku<anchor n="7"/> cēeyō ṭuṟṟa cūḷē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="2">Yesterday, in the new flood revered as pretty sweetness,</l>
        <l corresp="1">on the long dark expanse risen so as to reach the branches,</l>
        <l corresp="3">embracing a raft at the top, like a much-frenzied elephant bull,</l>
        <l corresp="5">removing [your] wet ornaments along with young companionable women</l>
        <l corresp="4">with thick dark tresses fragrant of bitter orange,</l>
        <l>you being without restraint in glancing [back] whenever the rain eyes</l>
        <l corresp="6f">of [the girl with] eminent grace glanced [at you] who moved [and] played in the water,</l>
        <l corresp="8">because passion was overpowering you lost [your] shame</l>
        <l corresp="9">[and] played [with them], they say of the delightful man. That,</l>
        <l corresp="15a-c">it has become a scandal as big</l>
        <l corresp="14">as the hum, on the day of great rice together with toddy </l>
        <l corresp="13">there in Arimaṇalvāyil Uṟattūr,</l>
        <l corresp="12">of those endowed with big ornaments who had curbed the great force</l>
        <l corresp="11">of the foes under the command of Evvi with sharp sword,</l>
        <l corresp="10">master of Nīṭūr with harp-sounding streets.</l>
        <l rend="indent5" corresp="15d">Now that,</l>
        <l corresp="16a-c">was no distress to us,</l>
        <l corresp="21">[but] the oath we had heard along with the much-fighting Red one,</l>
        <l corresp="20">at Ilaivāy with brilliant jewel lamps,</l>
        <l corresp="18">where the peacock that had flown up, frightened by the reverberating sound</l>
        <l corresp="16df">that was raised, the uproar being spectacular, by the ploughmen on the paddy fields, who are strong,</l>
        <l corresp="19">came [and] perched luxuriantly inside the awe-inspiring enclosure.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
